                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "06d67339-7a5b-341e-bed1-10e7a98f0747",
                        "entry_id": "fd5b6fc3-0bd7-3cb0-a0c8-1e3338b816f4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The place where a spring breaks out of the ground; the source of water for a stream or well."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a4508c71-7a21-455f-b046-15c3120c0c79",
                                "sense_id": "06d67339-7a5b-341e-bed1-10e7a98f0747",
                                "text": "Leaue the troubled streames,\nAnd liue as Thriuers doe at the Well head."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ed9f5ac7-0972-4304-b3e9-6e0904ecf45c",
                                "sense_id": "06d67339-7a5b-341e-bed1-10e7a98f0747",
                                "text": "It is a singular circumstance, that within a quarter of a mile of the well-head of the Wye, arises the Severn."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "37153a3d-3b1b-4516-b5da-c82c4be901a3",
                                "sense_id": "06d67339-7a5b-341e-bed1-10e7a98f0747",
                                "text": "We set forth accordingly by this itinerary; and for the best part of three nights travelled on eerie mountains and among the well-heads of wild rivers; [...]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ad314f90-2e17-3d66-a610-7e875e7abcd2",
                        "entry_id": "fd5b6fc3-0bd7-3cb0-a0c8-1e3338b816f4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The source of something; a fountainhead."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5524fb9e-f93c-45e8-92c1-dc77e463f1a3",
                                "sense_id": "ad314f90-2e17-3d66-a610-7e875e7abcd2",
                                "text": "[H]e likened was to a welhed / Of euill words, and wicked ſclaunders by him ſhed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b2275ef3-61ff-4de7-b58e-6b32c98131c7",
                                "sense_id": "ad314f90-2e17-3d66-a610-7e875e7abcd2",
                                "text": "[...] a bull was not merely a stud animal worth so much, due to go to the butcher in a little while. It was a vast wonder-beast, a well-head of the great, furnace-like passion that makes the worlds roll and the sun surge up [...]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "447faa1d-f93c-3322-bbbf-ead8b4f1d0ea",
                        "entry_id": "fd5b6fc3-0bd7-3cb0-a0c8-1e3338b816f4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The surface structure of an oil well etc."
